<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">armor</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">Armor</ansi> reduces the physical damage you take from
attacks. Your total physical defense comes from three
sources:

<ansi fg="yellow">1. Equipment</ansi>
  Worn gear (body armor, helmets, shields, etc.) provides
  damage reduction. Better equipment absorbs more damage.
  A shield in your off-hand provides an additional bonus.

<ansi fg="yellow">2. Natural Armor</ansi>
  Some creatures possess innate toughness -- thick hides,
  bony plates, or other natural protection.

<ansi fg="yellow">3. Magical Effects</ansi>
  Certain spells and enchantments can temporarily bolster
  your defenses against physical harm.

Mental attacks bypass physical armor entirely. Your
<ansi fg="command">Willpower</ansi> stat is your defense against those.

